    "lex": "BM25 over the shared document text. Documents and raw queries tokenized with Unicode alphanumeric runs excluding underscore, lowercased, common stopwords removed, and mapped through frozen corpus-lexicon.json.gz forms if present. Unique query terms. k1=1.2, b=0.75, idf=ln(1+(N-df+0.5)/(df+0.5)). Stable ties follow package/manifest order.",
    "stopwords": "a aby albo ale ani bo by czy dla do i ich ile jak jest już kiedy lub ma mi mój na nie o od oraz po pod przy się ta tak ten to u w we z za ze że",
    "dense": "Local INT8 ONNX on CPU, two intra-op threads and one inter-op thread. Prefix passage: for documents and query: for questions including Polish. Masked mean pooling and L2 normalization for both, exact float32 inner-product scan in stable manifest order. Batches of eight sorted by tokenized length. Limit 512 tokens.",
    "projected": "publicQuestion from frozen code. All eight had a public canonical projection. Raw calibration questions were processed locally. Only the public canonical text and 20 deterministic point IDs per question reached the staging reader.",
    "hybrid": "20 BM25 and 20 dense candidates, stable reciprocal rank fusion with weight 1/(zeroBasedRank+2), lexical list first on ties, top five. Identical BM25 list in each local and cloud hybrid. Local dense and hybrid use raw questions unless labeled Projected.",
    "cloud": "Actual qdrantKnowledgeSearch on the v4 staging collection using the frozen hybrid branch. 8 dense queries and 8 point-read requests. Both channels checked point UUID, corpus version, fragment SHA-256 and validity at read time. Supplied BM25 candidates isolate backend differences from runtime routing.",
    "runtimeCrossPackLexical": "Separate comparator: searchCorpus(rawQuestion) without a static route. Its confidence threshold can return an empty ranking. The actual answer service can also use curated routes, so this column does not estimate end-to-end answer quality.",
    "scoring": "Exact IDs and equivalent alternatives listed in existing qrels only. At least one alternative per required group; allGroupsAt5 requires all groups for the case. anyAt1/5 counts cases containing any accepted ID. mrrAt5 uses first accepted rank and zero for misses."
